              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a wholesaler, then the Persian for a retailer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: جنس",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جنس (jens) — \"material; goods, stock; a kind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جنس (jens) این پیراهن پنبه است. Jens-e in pirâhan panbe ast. This shirt is made of cotton."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic plural ajnâs 'goods'. Jens-e khub — good-quality goods."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jens was borrowed from Arabic jins 'kind, sort' (EtymDB). In Persian it came to mean the stuff a thing is made of, and goods for sale."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
