          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کالا (kâlâ) — \"goods, a product, a commodity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کالاهای این فروشگاه همه خارجی است. Kâlâ-hâ-ye in forushgâh hame khâreji ast. The goods in this shop are all foreign."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal; kâlâ-ye irâni — goods made at home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of kâlâ is not settled, and EtymDB does not list it. It is the usual word for goods in trade and in the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
